  "steps": [
    {
      "file": "Assets/Scripts/Board/Hex.cs",
      "description": "Make OnHeroUnplaced() too. Activate when the player move the hero out.\r\nIt should contain logic for untracking the hero on the board.\r\n\r\nIs that make sense?\r\n\r\n---\r\n**Reply:** Yes - implemented as Placement.OnHeroUnplaced(Hero) so both Hex and BenchSlot get a counterpart, wired into Preparation.MoveThisHeroInPreParationState before the new placement takes over.",
      "line": 33
    },
    {
      "file": "Assets/Scripts/Board/Hex.cs",
      "description": "what about setcurrenthex = null?\r\nIt use to exist, right?\r\n\r\n---\r\n**Reply:** It used to exist back when CurrentHex was its own independently-stored field. Now GetCurrentHex() is derived from CurrentPlacement, and OnHeroUnplaced is always immediately followed by the new placement's OnHeroPlaced (which overwrites CurrentPlacement) - so there's no window where a stale value would be observed. Nothing left to null.",
      "line": 40
    },
    {
      "file": "Assets/Scripts/Hero/HeroDataInCombat.cs",
      "description": "I want to change the name to \"HeroDataRuntime\".\r\nAnd contain every run time data for each hero.\r\n\r\nSo this data should also have _currentPlacement;\r\n\r\nIs that make sense?\r\n\r\n---\r\n**Reply:** Yes - ReservedHex (where the hero wants to go) already lived here, so CurrentPlacement (where it currently is) belongs alongside it instead of one level up in the Blackboard. Renamed the file/class to HeroDataRuntime and moved CurrentPlacement in.",
      "line": 3
    },
    {
      "file": "Assets/Scripts/Core/GameManager.cs",
      "description": "Use new input system, specifically the playerinputsystem we have.",
      "line": 22
    }
  ]
